<title>NEW ZEALAND: Mercury withdraws all offers for PNZ shrs.</title>
<headline>Mercury withdraws all offers for PNZ shrs.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unlisted Auckland-based electricity supplier Mercury Energy said on Tuesday it had withdrawn all of its offers for shares in Power New Zealand.  </p>
<p>Mercury, for more than two years, has been locked in a battle with U.S.-based UtiliCorp United Inc for control of its fellow Auckland electricity distributor.</p>
<p>Mercury has around 31 percent of Power NZ while Utilicorp, through Utilicorp New Zealand Ltd, around 28 percent.</p>
<p>Spokesmen for all three parties were not immediately available for comment on the latest developments.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
</text>
